GLOSSARY = {
    "Drought risk score (0 to 100)": "How likely crops on this plot are to suffer from drought in the coming weeks. Higher is worse. Under 36 is low, 36 to 69 is moderate, 70 and above is high.",
    "Crop health outlook (VCI)": "How healthy and green the crop cover is compared with normal for this time of year, from 0 to 100. Higher is better. Below 35 means drought stress. Note this runs the opposite way to the risk score.",
    "Forecast range": "The band the outlook will most likely fall in. About 8 times out of 10, the real value lands inside it.",
    "Rain deficit (SPEI)": "Whether recent rain has been too low for what crops need, after counting the water that heat evaporates. The 14d and 30d versions look back two and four weeks.",
    "Crop stress signal (NDRE)": "A satellite reading of leaf chlorophyll. It drops before leaves visibly yellow, which is why it works as an early warning.",
    "Greenness (NDVI)": "A satellite reading of how dense and green the crop cover is.",
    "Dry air (VPD)": "How dry the air is. Drier air pulls more water out of plants.",
    "Soil moisture stress (ESI)": "How much water plants are actually getting compared with what they need.",
    "Heat build-up (GDD)": "Heat accumulated over the season. Too much heat above what the crop tolerates adds stress.",
    "Backtest": "A forecast made for a past date, so it can be checked against what really happened.",
}
